<!-- file-explorer-pal.xhtpm - real, shared File Explorer widget.
     11.brainstorm/2026-09-05/PDL-READER-AND-FILE-EXPLORER-WIDGET.md.

     Static template + real manager (file_explorer_manager.+x, a
     <module>), same house convention every other widget this session
     touched already uses (taskbar-settings, swatch-picker, open-hai).
     The manager owns the actual directory scan/navigation/pick state
     and publishes it as file_explorer_ui.txt; this template only
     ever renders whatever it published, via vars=.

     REAL FIX 2026-09-05, found live testing this exact window twice:
     vars= resolves a relative token against g_package_dir (this
     widget's OWN directory, since that's where this file lives) -
     just the bare filename is correct here, not a path repeating
     this widget's own directory a second time.

     FE_ENTRY:<n> / FE_SAVEAS / FE_CANCEL / FE_CRUMB:<n> are real,
     generic dispatch verbs khtpm_core_render.c's own dispatch()
     handles in-process (same exact "write an incrementing-seq action
     file the manager polls" convention PICK:<n> already uses for
     taskbar-settings) - not a launched shell relay script, which
     would have no reliable way to know its own absolute install path
     from inside a static template.

     SAVE mode's filename field is a real, generic <cli_io> - typing
     into it is handled entirely by the shared renderer itself
     (default_cli_io_handle_key(), this session's own real cursor
     work). FE_SAVEAS reads this field's LIVE value directly off the
     tree (dispatch()'s own find_by_id("filename")) rather than a
     `${filename}` substitution, which would only ever reflect the
     manager's last-published value, not every keystroke.
     show="${show_save_row}" hides the whole row in LOAD mode (manager
     publishes show_save_row=0/1 based on its own mode=).

     REAL RESHAPE 2026-09-15, direct live pushback ("wait. requires a
     sidebar? thats insane" / "plenty of our layouts, like emojis
     palettes dont have sidebar... if ur saying sidebar is needed for
     resizing thats a different legacy bug that we can remove") -
     this file used to be sidebar+panel-shaped ONLY because that was
     the one real layout path this renderer had with working real
     scrolling for a plain vertical list - confirmed by direct code
     read: palettes-emojis.xhtpm proves a flat <page> with NO sidebar/
     panel already gets real chrome + real width via a completely
     separate "swatch-grid" layout path, but that path is a multi-
     column tile grid, a genuine mismatch for a text list; the OTHER
     real flat-page path (plain context menus etc.) had zero
     <scrolllist> support at all - a <scrolllist> there silently
     matched no tag case and its children were simply never laid out.
     Real fix, not a per-widget workaround: khtpm_core_render.c's flat-
     page path now has real <scrolllist> support (delegates to
     layout_scroll_region(), the same generic primitive the sidebar+
     panel path already used) and its own <tabbar> layout is no longer
     canvas-only - both real, generic renderer fixes, not specific to
     this file. This template now uses them directly: no <sidebar>, no
     <panel>, just <tabbar> (breadcrumbs) + a real top-level
     <scrolllist> that fills the rest of the window. -->

<window label="File Explorer - ${mode}" class="file-explorer-pal database-window user-resizable" vars="file_explorer_ui.txt" drop_highlight="#88ff66" drop_action="sh -c 'exec sh &quot;$1/&amp;.widgits/file-explorer/ops/fe_drop.sh&quot; &quot;$0&quot; &quot;$1&quot;'">
  <!-- REAL, NEW 2026-09-05 - launch_module() passes house_root then
       package_dir automatically, then this <module>'s own id= as a
       THIRD, single extra argv slot (kh_collect_and_launch_modules()'s
       own real convention - id doubles as extra_arg when set, same as
       every other module-launching widget in the house). That extra
       slot carries the browse mode; the manager always starts
       browsing at house_root itself (a real, honest v1 default - see
       file_explorer_manager.c's own header for why a configurable
       start_dir isn't wired up yet). -->
  <module src="&.widgits/file-explorer/ops/+x/file_explorer_manager.+x" id="LOAD"/>
  <page name="main">
    <!-- 2026-09-18: do NOT put an <item id="chrome-close"> here.
         Grid mode (any class="swatch") synthesizes g_default_close_elem
         already; list/flat does too when found_close is 0. An extra
         template X was laid as a chip ([ ]1) beside the real chrome X
         ([ ]100) — never intended. Auto chrome only. -->
    <tabbar class="fe-crumbs-bar">
      <repeat count="${n_crumbs}" bind="crumb">
      <tab id="crumb${crumb.#}" label="${crumb.label}" action="FE_CRUMB:${crumb.#}"/>
      </repeat>
    </tabbar>
    <!-- REAL, NEW 2026-09-15, direct live report ("can the back button
         and grid view be on same row, instead of back being tied to
         other files? get it?") - Back is no longer a synthetic row
         inside the file list (file_explorer_manager.c's own header
         comment on list_directory() has the full real story); it's its
         own toolbar item next to the grid/list toggle, dispatched via
         FE_BACK (generic FE_ prefix -> cmd="BACK", handled directly in
         the manager). show="${has_back}" hides it at the real root
         (has_back = current_dir != "/"). -->
    <item id="back" class="opacity-btn" show="${has_back}" action="FE_BACK" label="⬅️ Back"/>
    <item id="viewtoggle" class="opacity-btn" action="FE_VIEWMODE" label="${view_toggle_label}"/>
    <text label="Pick a file to load." class="quiet" show="${show_load_hint}"/>
    <cli_io id="filename" target_id="filename" label="Save as: " show="${show_save_row}"/>
    <item id="save" class="opacity-btn" show="${show_save_row}" action="FE_SAVEAS" label="Save"/>
    <scrolllist show="${is_list_view}">
      <repeat count="${n_entries}" bind="entry">
      <item id="entry${entry.#}" class="fe-entry sprite-inline" sprite="${entry.sprite}" action="FE_ENTRY:${entry.#}" label="${entry.icon}  ${entry.name} ${entry.size}"/>
      </repeat>
    </scrolllist>
    <!-- REAL, NEW 2026-09-15, direct live request ("we wanted list/grid
         toggle remember?") - reuses the renderer's own real swatch-grid
         layout path (palettes-emojis.xhtpm's own proven shape), not a
         new mechanism. Real, honest limitation, found live while
         building this: that path is WHOLE-PAGE (triggers the instant
         any real <item class="swatch"> exists anywhere in the page,
         not per-region), and has no <tabbar>/<scrolllist> handling of
         its own - so grid mode's own count (n_grid_entries, file_
         explorer_manager.c) is genuinely 0 whenever list mode is
         active (no swatch items exist in the tree at all then, so
         list mode's own tabbar+scrolllist render normally), and
         breadcrumbs/the close button's own real behavior in GRID mode
         specifically hasn't been proven live yet - test both modes
         before trusting this comment over what's actually on screen. -->
    <repeat count="${n_grid_entries}" bind="entry">
    <item id="gentry${entry.#}" class="swatch" sprite="${entry.sprite}" label="${entry.icon}  ${entry.name} ${entry.size}" action="FE_ENTRY:${entry.#}"/>
    </repeat>
  </page>
</window>
